# apollo routing

When the user says **`apollo`**, **`build apolyx`**, or clearly asks to implement / polish the Apolyx UI kit:

1. Load `.cursor/skills/apollo/SKILL.md` and `Docs/agents/apollo/instructions/00-workflow.md`
2. Open `Docs/feature_list/ui-kit/00-intent.md` first
3. Work in `elements/ui-kit` (package `@altr/apolyx`), `apps/apolyx`, `elements/apolyx-cli` as needed
4. Hard rules: no Radix / Base UI; themes `default` | `power-blue` | `power-green` × light/dark; charts = SVG + visx; monorepo = workspace import
5. Element deps: apolyx may use `@altr/base`; never depend on jord — `Docs/feature_list/00-elements-dependency-rules.md`
6. Load at most 1–3 companion skills (taste / React / Tailwind / Motion) — see `Docs/agents/apollo/skills/README.md`
7. After a non-trivial ship, route docs to **docs_man** (`update_docs`) unless already asked

Do not treat aesthetic `shadcn` skills as permission to add Radix.
